\end{equation*}

denote the group of all \emph{admissible color permutations} for $f_0$. Given some type $\tau$ and flags $F_1, F_2 \in \mathcal{F}^\tau$, we say they are \emph{generalized isomorphic} with respect to $f_0$, denoted by $F_1 \simeq_g F_2$, if there exists $\alpha \in \Upsilon$ and $\beta: [v(\tau)] \overset{\sim}{\hookrightarrow} [v(\tau)]$ satisfying $\pi^{(\alpha,\beta)}(F_1) \simeq F_2$. For each flag $F$, we will let $\mu(F)$ denote an arbitrary but canonical representative of the equivalence class induced by $\simeq_g$.  We also let

